[[0,1352754,0,1,1,0,"2016-10-18T00:54:53","SavedGameStudios","",[],"","My Channel On Vid.Me and a brief introduction to everyone (in the comments)","https://vid.me/SavedGameStudios","letsplay"],[1,6589383,0,2,0,2,"2016-10-18T00:57:02","SavedGameStudios","",[],"<p>Hello everyone! I am escaping the absolute hell holes of YouTube and Reddit over here on VidMe and now on Voat! I look forward to seeing everyone's stuff and I appreciate any time people take out of their busy lives to check out my stuff!</p>\n<p>I've been doing this for about a year and a half now, so if anyone has questions, likes what I do and wants to know how I do it... just ask. I love talking about mics and OBS and Lightworks and Audacity and compressors and equalizers and all of that stuff!</p>\n<p>See everyone around!</p>"]]
[[0,1352755,0,4,0,4,"2016-10-18T00:55:07","Disappointed","",[],"","UK Tribunal Says Spy Agencies Illegally Collected Communications Data In Bulk For More Than A Decade","https://www.techdirt.com/articles/20161017/08014035820/uk-tribunal-says-spy-agencies-illegally-collected-communications-data-bulk-more-than-decade.shtml","technology"],[1,6590059,0,4,0,4,"2016-10-18T02:31:29","PM_ME_UR_NOODZ","",[],"<p>Why is that headline in the past tense? </p>"],[2,6590405,6590059,6,0,6,"2016-10-18T03:20:42","Apathy","",[],"<p>Well they used to do it, I mean they still do it, but they used to as well. </p>"],[1,6590659,0,2,2,0,"2016-10-18T03:56:06","Driveby_Dogboy","",[],"<p>Yeah, we're not going to stop either.</p>"],[1,6593102,0,1,0,1,"2016-10-18T14:31:54","elgindelta","",[],"<p>It's called spying. That's what you do</p>"],[2,6596918,6593102,2,1,1,"2016-10-18T23:28:46","Disappointed","",[],"<p>Spying on your citizens. Correct. </p>"],[3,6597868,6596918,1,0,1,"2016-10-19T01:54:14","elgindelta","",[],"<p>Yea, cuz they totes respected the borders. </p>"],[4,6600081,6597868,1,1,0,"2016-10-19T10:10:40","Disappointed","",[],"<p>You kinda lost me. I think were talking about two different things or coming at it from a different angle. Have a vote anyway.</p>"],[5,6603248,6600081,1,0,1,"2016-10-19T19:13:51","elgindelta","",[],"<p>Thought you were saying that from the UK side. The legal hurdles of domestic syping were circumvented via agreements between the US and UK originally by the UK spying on the US citizenry and vise versa. This way the data was in hand without oversight or liability. It's interesting to note the practice has been in play much longer than the public knows. Data centers have been around and grown as the tech to accommodate the task has evolved. Project Echelon was initiated in 1966 and brought online in 1974. </p>\n<p><a href=\"http://www.whatreallyhappened.com/RANCHO/POLITICS/ECHELON/echelon.html\">http://www.whatreallyhappened.com/RANCHO/POLITICS/ECHELON/echelon.html</a></p>\n<p>The real kicker is that it's to much data to be reliably scoured by even an army of analyst's. </p>\n<p><a href=\"http://electrospaces.blogspot.com/2014/06/some-numbers-about-nsas-data-collection.html?m=1\">http://electrospaces.blogspot.com/2014/06/some-numbers-about-nsas-data-collection.html?m=1</a></p>\n<p>And yet is dumped and stored at data sites across the globe. What then, could possibly be reading the rhythm? Lulz, a tin foil hat answer for another time. Point, it has been and will continue, being far deeper in scope than acknowledged ever. </p>"],[6,6604428,6603248,1,1,0,"2016-10-19T21:56:05","Disappointed","",[],"<p>I agree. </p>"]]
